# Product and design contracts

- An approved specification under `tasks/specs/` is the source of truth for
  feature behavior, routes, content, claims, integrations, business rules,
  and visual acceptance criteria.
- `docs/product.md` records durable product-wide decisions.
- `docs/design.md` records durable visual decisions when a project adopts a
  design system or approved reference.
- `docs/api.md` and `docs/database.md` record the consolidated HTTP and
  persistent-data contracts.
- Treat an empty or `TBD` business or security field as undecided. Ask the
  human instead of inventing a requirement, persona, route, copy, metric,
  integration, or security policy. Decide missing design and technical how
  as a senior engineer, record it in the specification, and promote
  recurring visual decisions into `docs/design.md`.
- Implement PWA, authentication, responsive targets, and external services
  only when the approved specification and relevant global contract require
  them.
- Update the relevant global contract when an approved feature changes a
  durable decision.
